{
  "_": "The world's components and the models that draw them, one place (realistic.gd reads it through data.gd; docs/TUNING.md). A placer asks for a component (fence, house_poor, keep...), never a file, so a new art family is an edit here. Shape: Paradox's entity files and RimWorld's ThingDef graphicData. Per component: kind (what the town rules ask for: house, hall, barn, prop, clutter...) and variants. Per variant: model (under res://assets; a folder means its scene.gltf), name (the name placers used before the catalogue, kept while they move over), length (its true longest side in metres: the scale), height (its true height in metres, used for the scale instead when the length misleads: a tall stack, a lying cluster), and optionally strip (parts the land supplies itself), floorCut (game units: triangles under it dropped), stone (no glow), weight (how often it's picked). Order matters: it is the order placers pick in. heightRange: the true height a component should stand, in metres (lowest, highest): tools/scale_check.gd fails a model outside it (a hut must never stand as tall as a castle tower).",
  "woods": {
    "_": "Which trees the woods grow (forest.gd). set: pack (the realistic pine, oak and bush packs) or kit (Quaternius Stylized Nature, the painted look); --trees=pack or --trees=kit overrides. kit: per role (pine, oak, bush) the model files and the true height in metres a grown one stands; young and sapling: how tall the younger trees are, as a share of grown.",
    "set": "pack",
    "kit": {
      "pine": { "models": ["nature/Pine_1.gltf", "nature/Pine_2.gltf", "nature/Pine_3.gltf", "nature/Pine_4.gltf", "nature/Pine_5.gltf"], "height": 17.0 },
      "oak": { "models": ["nature/CommonTree_1.gltf", "nature/CommonTree_2.gltf", "nature/CommonTree_3.gltf", "nature/CommonTree_4.gltf", "nature/CommonTree_5.gltf", "nature/TwistedTree_1.gltf", "nature/TwistedTree_3.gltf"], "height": 15.0 },
      "bush": { "models": ["nature/Bush_Common.gltf", "nature/Bush_Common_Flowers.gltf"], "height": 1.6 },
      "young": 0.65,
      "sapling": 0.35
    }
  },
